### 2026-02-12 -- Replace aggregated curve_fit with per-record logistic regression inference

- Reworked half-life fitting from `scipy.optimize.curve_fit` on aggregated
  sweep pass-rate points to `statsmodels.Logit` on pooled non-empty binary
  sweep records per directive.
- `scores.json` half-life entries now include inferential fields:
  - slope/intercept terms (`beta0`, `beta1`) and uncertainty
    (`beta1_se`, `beta1_pvalue`)
  - likelihood-ratio test against a flat (intercept-only) model
    (`lr_statistic`, `lr_pvalue`)
  - fitted half-life confidence interval
    (`x_half_ci_lower`, `x_half_ci_upper`)
  - non-empty sample counts (`n_observations`, `n_pass`, `n_fail`)
- Added fit-status handling for perfect compliance/failure, convergence
  failures, non-significant/no-decay patterns, and beyond-range half-life.
- Updated `report.py` half-life table columns to show beta slope, p-values,
  LR-test p-value, fitted half-life CI, and non-empty sample size.
- Added `statsmodels` dependency in `requirements.txt`.
- Files touched: `halflifebench/scorer.py`, `halflifebench/report.py`,
  `requirements.txt`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/claude.mdc`.
- User-visible: report + scores now include statistical decay evidence and
  confidence intervals, not just descriptive fitted half-life values.

